              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\frac{\\log(a)}{\\log(b)}=\\log(a)-\\log(b)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "False",
                  "width": 18
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "A quotient of logarithms is not the subtraction law. For example, take $a=b=10$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\log(10)}{\\log(10)}&=1\\\\\\log(10)-\\log(10)&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q2",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p20-q2-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\log(a)+\\log(b)=\\log(ab)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "True",
                  "width": 18
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "The addition law gives $\\log(a)+\\log(b)=\\log(ab)$ for positive $a$ and $b$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q3",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p20-q3-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\log(a)\\log(b)=\\log(a+b)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "False",
                  "width": 18
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "There is no logarithmic law of this form. For example, take $a=b=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log(1)\\log(1)&=0\\\\\\log(1+1)&=\\log(2)\\ne0.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q4",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p20-q4-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\bigl(\\log_b(a)\\bigr)^n=n\\log_b(a)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "False",
                  "width": 18
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "The power law is $\\log_b(a^n)=n\\log_b(a)$; the exponent must be on the argument. For example, with $a=b=10$ and $n=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\bigl(\\log_{10}(10)\\bigr)^2&=1\\\\2\\log_{10}(10)&=2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p20-q5-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\log\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)=\\log(a)-\\log(b)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "True",
                  "width": 18
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "The subtraction law gives $\\log\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)=\\log(a)-\\log(b)$ for positive $a$ and $b$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
